# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Identities allowed on commits (author and committer), checked by hack/git-identity-check.sh in the
# lane worktrees' hooks and in CI. One `Name <email>` shell glob per line.
#
# Who may add lines: only a maintainer. A person does not need one: they commit under their GitHub
# noreply address (`<id>+<username>@users.noreply.github.com`), which the last line allows.
# CI reads this list from the pull request's base, so a pull request cannot widen its own list.
#
# Agent identities: the project identity below (agents and lanes work under it), or the noreply
# address of the human the agent works for.

# The project identity (agents and lanes).
procoduck <coder@procodus.dev>

# GitHub-attributed identities: web UI commits and merges, the merge queue, bots, and contributors
# who use their GitHub noreply address. The `* <*@users.noreply.github.com>` line allows ANY name with a
# GitHub noreply address on purpose: a web edit, "Update branch" or a bot commit carries the account's
# display name, which this list cannot know. It is an attribution guard against a personal name from a
# global git config, not an access control (that is branch protection and review).
GitHub <noreply@github.com>
* <*@users.noreply.github.com>
